// =============================================================================
// MM Audio-Injection Subsystem — NO-OP STUBS
// =============================================================================
// Audio injection is redundant in 2ship (native MM audio) — no-op stub, mirrors
// mm_bgm_loader.cpp.
//
// The original SoH-style subsystem here decoded MM ADPCM samples, patched
// SoundFont sample pointers, and mixed MM SFX directly into the audio output.
// It depended on SoH audio-engine types/members that DO NOT exist in 2ship
// (SoundFontSample, SoundFontSound, Instrument.lowNotesSound/normalNotesSound/
// highNotesSound, Drum.sound, SoundEffect.sample, OTRAudio_LockMutex/UnlockMutex,
// etc.). In 2ship the game already IS Majora's Mask, so its sound effects play
// natively and this cross-game injection path is unnecessary.
//
// Every entry point below keeps its EXACT signature so all callers still link
// (the public MmSfx_*/MmDirectAudio_*/MmGakki_* API declared in mm_asset_loader.h,
// plus the MmSfxBridge_*/MmSfxDecode_Sample bridge entrypoints used by the
// mods/sound_translator engine). Each simply returns a benign value / does
// nothing. If native-bypass MM SFX injection is ever needed again, re-port the
// engine against 2ship's audio/lib types (audio/soundfont.h uses Sample /
// TunedSample instead of SoundFontSample / SoundFontSound).
//
// The archive / texture / skeleton / display-list asset loaders ABOVE and BELOW
// this block are the real reason this file exists and are fully retained.
// =============================================================================

// True when MM audio is available. Stubbed to 0 so callers take their native /
// vanilla audio path instead of the (removed) MM-injection path.
s32 MmSfx_IsAvailable(void) {
    return 0;
}

